<DocsLayout title="Strands Agents guide | Agent-Gantry" description="Integrate Agent-Gantry with AWS Strands Agents: per-turn tool selection through BeforeModelCallEvent, error ToolResults, approval through Strands interrupts, and the tool context.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Framework guide</p>
  <h1>AWS Strands Agents</h1>
  <p class="lead">Agent-Gantry plugs into Strands' own mechanisms: a <code>BeforeModelCallEvent</code> hook that picks each model call's tools, error <code>ToolResult</code>s for failures, Strands interrupts for human approval, and the <code>ToolContext</code> for your run state.</p>
  <p><a class="pill" href="/Agent-Gantry/docs/frameworks/strands/advanced/">Advanced Strands usage →</a></p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`uv add "agent-gantry[strands]"   # strands-agents >= 1.38`} />

  <h2>Basic page: tools picked every model call</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="python" code={`from agent_gantry import AgentGantry
from agent_gantry.strands import StrandsAdapter

gantry = AgentGantry()

@gantry.register(examples=["where is my order", "has order 4471 shipped"])
def get_order_status(order_id: str) -> str:
    """Return the current shipping status for an order."""
    return "in_transit"

await gantry.sync()
agent = StrandsAdapter(gantry).agent(limit=5)     # Bedrock by default; pass model=... for others
result = await agent.invoke_async("Has order 4471 shipped?")`} />
  <p>For a fixed set, pass <code>Agent(tools=await adapter.select(query))</code> instead.</p>

  <h2>What the model sees when a tool fails</h2>
  <p>A failed call returns <code>&#123;"status": "error", "content": [&#123;"text": "&lt;type&gt;: &lt;message&gt;"&#125;]&#125;</code>, capped at 2,000 characters, so the model can correct a bad argument or try something else.</p>
  <div class="callout"><strong>Redact or opt out:</strong> <code>StrandsAdapter(gantry, error_formatter=redact)</code> rewrites the text; <code>error_mode="raise"</code> raises <code>ToolExecutionError</code> instead.</div>

  <h2>Reading run state from a Gantry tool</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="python" code={`from agent_gantry.strands import current_tool_context

@gantry.register
def get_balance(account: str) -> str:
    """Fetch an account balance for the signed-in user."""
    ctx = current_tool_context()            # Strands ToolContext, or None outside a run
    return bank.balance(ctx.invocation_state["user"], account)

# await agent.invoke_async("What's my balance?", user=current_user)`} />
